BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zine Making Workshop
DTSTART:20260821T200000Z
DTEND:20260821T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260821T060148Z
UID:11c91c57-eb63-5c5f-85b7-d974caaebb09
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Cycle Toronto Rec Hub for a hands-on Zine Makin
 g Workshop\, where you'll learn to fold\, cut\, and assemble a punk zine u
 sing the classic one-fold\, one-cut method. This session covers everything
  from the DIY ethos and history of zines to planning your content\, adding
  collage or drawings\, and finishing your creation. No experience or speci
 al tools are needed. Just bring your ideas\, and leave with new skills and
  a completed zine.\n\nDoors: 4 PM\n\nSession: 4:00-6:00 PM\n\n"SF punk zin
 es at Prelinger Library" by Lindsay Eyink is licensed under CC BY 2.0. (ht
 tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zine#/media/File:SF_punk_zines_at_Prelinger_Li
 brary.jpg) Source: Wikimedia Commons\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca/zine_mak
 ing_workshop
LOCATION:Evergreen Brickworks\n550 Bayview Ave\n10\nToronto  ON M4W 3X8\nC
 A
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/zine_making_workshop
END:VEVENT
